No, don't replace catalina.sh with bash.

I was giving CMD ["bash"] only as an example of a possible mistake that can cause a container to exit.

For a Tomcat application, your Dockerfile should look like:

Dockerfile
FROM tomcat:9.0
 
COPY target/*.war /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT.war
 
EXPOSE 8080
 
CMD ["catalina.sh", "run"]

catalina.sh run is correct because it keeps Tomcat running in the foreground.

